  intro:'This lesson teaches the whole tooth check-up, step by step, so the chair feels like a game before the real visit.',
  what:'A dentist’s office is where teeth get their check-ups: counted, cleaned, and protected from sugar bugs.',
  mean:'Small habits, big teeth: the dentist is the coach who helps your smile win every day.',
  know:'You need brave sitting, an open mouth on request, and a toothbrush working at home twice a day — the dentist sees everything, you know.',
  why:'Teeth are the only bones we show the world — and the only ones that can get holes. The dentist finds tiny trouble while it is still tiny.',
  dev:'Opening wide on request, sitting in a chair that leans, naming teeth (front, pointy, big grinders), and the twice-a-day brushing habit.',
  vocab:'dentist, teeth, tooth, check-up, mirror, polish, sugar bugs, sticker, open wide',
  teach:'1) Climb into the big chair — it leans back like a rocket ready for launch.\n2) Open wide and say ahh — the little mirror hops in for a look around.\n3) Count the teeth out loud: how many live in there today?\n4) Hunt for sugar bugs — spot them before they build a house.\n5) Polish! The spinning brush tickles, the teeth shine, and the treasure box pays out the sticker.',
  say:'"Hop in the chair, open wide — AHH! The dentist counts: one, two, three... all here! No sugar bugs today! Now the polish — bzzzz — tickle, tickle — all shiny! Sticker, please!"',
