  teach:'1) See the badge — a star on a shield — the same star officers wear on their chest and their patrol car.\n2) Officers start the day here: roll call, radio check, and off into the town.\n3) Lost things come here: bicycles, gloves, teddy bears — the shelf waits patiently.\n4) If a child is lost, the plan is simple and strong: find a police officer (or a parent with children), say your name and your grown-up’s name, and stay together until found.\n5) The station never closes — somebody is there right now, tonight, and every night.',
