  ask:'"Who works at the police station?" (police officers) "What does the badge mean?" (you can ask me for help) "What do we say if we are lost?" (our name and our grown-up’s name)',
  childSay:'Your child might badge every drawing with a star and shield, radio the dinner table ("officer requesting snacks"), or practice the lost-plan on every walk — pointing out officers and whispering "helpers".',
  real:'In the US, UK and Canada the lost-child plan is the same: find a police officer or a parent with children and say your name. Practicing it as a game turns the scariest moment into a known routine — that is this card’s whole job.',
  play:'The friendly-officer game: one toy walks a cushion street and gets "lost"; the officer asks kindly questions — name, who we are looking for — and walks everyone home. Reunion hug required by law.',
